        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>As <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/2321243/im-ditching-my-passwords-you-should-too.html\">I\u2019ve said before</a>, passwords suck. So do made-up holidays, but World Password Day (which rolls around yearly on May 1) offers as good excuse as any to kick your passwords to the curb.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Sure, the holiday\u2019s intent is getting you to update your passwords to be more secure\u2014like finally abandoning <em>password12345</em> (oof) for <em>XSmpJAI5v@NtG-7L#Q2F</em>. Or, if passphrases are more your vibe, <em>Water-Whom-Atom-Flame-Snake5</em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>But to heck with updating. Go with <em>replacing</em>. Specifically, replacing your passwords with passkeys.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Passkeys don\u2019t require memorization, can be stored directly on your phone, <em>and</em> are stronger than passwords. One particular advantage: They\u2019re phishing-resistant. Also, if a website gets",
